Wrote the bug-reproducing test to `src/hello.test.ts`.

The test mirrors the repo's existing Vitest style exactly (same imports, `describe`/`it`/`expect` structure) and asserts the observable greeting behavior:

1. **`returns hello dolly`** — asserts `getGreeting()` now produces the updated greeting. Against pre-fix code (returning `'hello world'`), this fails.
2. **`no longer returns the old hello world greeting`** — asserts the old text is gone entirely, so only the updated greeting is shown.

Both cases pass with the fix and fail without it.
